  (fn-do _ lay-capture LayoutId
    (param instance InstanceId)
    (param bound Binding)
    (param nested NestedFunction)
    ; A body that shares a name holds first the link to the environment in force where it was
    ; spawned, as a lambda written there is given. Then it holds what it copies, and the state of
    ; each global `do with` binds that the body holds, as it was where the task was spawned. The
    ; body of a `do without gc` block holds the address of each local and argument it refers to
    ; (`refers`), with the type of the value kept there.
